codex
D612’s hold on paid work stands, with the exposure correction recorded. I would not open a code check based on the six gate failures.

The correction does identify unread material for a future test. It does not resolve the comparison’s sample size or starting-library problems. The exposure check is also specifically a match against **Step 1 traces**; it does not by itself establish that those articles were unseen by every other activity. [Corrected feasibility review](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/comparison-feasibility/RESULT.md)

The six failures are not one malformed shape. In [the fourth reading](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_a/result-4/RESULT.md:37), they include a question that loses a distinction between two years, a “during 2028” condition widened to “by the end of 2028,” a restructuring treated as ruling out a deal, and three unjustified refusals. Detecting those generally requires interpreting what the question and answer mean; a check fitted to their words would take a judgment from the model and risk rejecting valid cases.

A2’s improvement on unlisted parts would not repair those **observed** misses: line 2 already met the 44-thesis gate. A change could still affect other lines, positively or negatively, but that is not a demonstrated candidate for passing the gate. D426 also explicitly stops further tuning on those 44 theses. [D426](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS.md:770)

I therefore see no sufficiently specified identity check to justify a new trace or implementation now. Reopen if a **general, independently evidenced structural contradiction** is identified—one that code can detect without deciding the question’s meaning and that is tested against valid counterexamples outside these six sends.

CONSENSUS: retain D612; correct D611’s exposure claim; no new check or paid send on the six failures.
